INT. STRIKE-N-SPARE BOWLING ALLEY - THANKSGIVING EVE

Lane 7 has been turned into a dinner table. Paper turkeys. Folding chairs. Ball returns hold gravy boats. A neon pin flashes overhead.

GRANDPA WALTER (80s, bowling shirt, thick glasses) sits at the head, carving. DOROTHEA (50s, pearls, tight smile) sets plates. HAL (50s, gravy-stained tie) fiddles with a ball polisher. LINUS (teen, headphones) slouches. SUNNY (8, pigtails, tiny bowling shoes) crawls under the table. IMOGEN (30s, tote bag, tired eyes) arrives late, pulling off a scarf.

DOROTHEA
Imogen, you said six.

IMOGEN
It's six-oh-four.

DOROTHEA
Grandpa has been carving for forty minutes.

GRANDPA WALTER
I like carving.

HAL
That's not what you said about the turkey last year.

GRANDPA WALTER
Last year the turkey was dry.

DOROTHEA
It was not dry.

HAL
It was a little dry, Dot.

DOROTHEA
Hal!

LINUS
Can I eat in the car?

DOROTHEA
No.

LINUS
Can I eat on the lane?

HAL
It's literally on the lane, Linus.

SUNNY
(from under the table)
Aunt Imogen, you have a hole in your sock.

IMOGEN
Thank you, Sunny.

DOROTHEA
Can we all sit, please?

GRANDPA WALTER
Sit. Eat. Say grace.

HAL
Who's saying grace?

DOROTHEA
Imogen, you say it.

IMOGEN
Me?

DOROTHEA
You're the one who left.

Silence. The pin on the ceiling flashes. Linus pulls off his headphones.

IMOGEN
That was unkind, Dorothea.

DOROTHEA
It was accurate.

HAL
Dot, let's not.

DOROTHEA
Nobody asked you, Harold.

GRANDPA WALTER
Girls, girls.

IMOGEN
We're not girls, Grandpa.

DOROTHEA
Speak for yourself.

SUNNY
Can I have pie?

LINUS
Nobody has pie, Sunny. We're in a war.

Dorothea slams the gravy boat on the table. Gravy leaps. It lands on Hal's tie. He stares at it.

HAL
Well, that's the last straw.

He stands. Flings a ball from the return. It rolls down Lane 7, scattering the cranberry and three chairs. Strike.

Everyone stares at the pins. Then at Grandpa Walter. He sets down the knife.

GRANDPA WALTER
Nice.

Linus snickers. Sunny giggles. Imogen covers her mouth. Dorothea tries to stay stern and fails. Hal bows.
